  "question": "Which explicit short-path families and critical-value estimates are proved for Erdős #1041, and which of those statements have Lean or Comparator checks?",
  "precis": "This note gives ordinary proofs for explicit short-path families, led by all-degree monic trinomials, and separately establishes a sharp critical-value mean. It records which subsidiary statements have Lean and Comparator checks. Exact obstruction examples show why the radial and critical-value estimates cannot be silently promoted to a general connector theorem. The work does not resolve unrestricted Erdős #1041; the recent degree-seven counterexample announcement is a separate external claim.",
